{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The HDMI cable feels useful alongside my TV and Blu-ray equipment because it helps connect what I already have; the ten-foot length makes it appealing as a spare.",
    "The microSD cards fit my history of removable storage and my card reader, although that makes them plausible future purchases rather than something I need now."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Fire TV sticks repeat a role my 4K Max bundle already fills, so sharing the same streaming features gives me little reason to choose them.",
    "The older Echo Dot and Echo Show feel unnecessary after my newer versions and recent Show stand purchase. The older tablet and wired earbuds also lack a clear connection to a current need."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My Alexa purchases seem to be taken as interest in any Alexa device, even when the suggested item is an older version of something I already have.",
    "My frequent electronics purchases seem to be treated as a reason to offer more devices, while I often buy accessories to support equipment I already use."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The specific generations I recently bought matter: another older speaker, display, or streaming stick does not offer a clear benefit for my setup.",
    "There is a difference between a useful accessory and an immediate need. I would choose the HDMI cable as a spare, but the storage cards would wait until I need more capacity."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You recognized my interest in electronics and Alexa, but missed that useful additions to my existing setup appeal more than older devices that duplicate it."
}"}
